<title>LITHUANIA: YIELD ON ONE-MONTH T-BILLS SLIPS.</title>
<headline>YIELD ON ONE-MONTH T-BILLS SLIPS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield for</p>
<p>Lithuanian Treasury bills fell to 8.49 percent at auction on</p>
<p>Tuesday from 9.33 percent at a sale of 27-day paper on December</p>
<p>17, the central bank said.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of litas.</p>
<p> MATURITY  AVG YIELD  LAST TIME  MIN/MAX   ISSUE  BID    SOLD</p>
<p> 28-day	8.49	 9.33    8.0/8.80     30  71.067  30</p>
<p>The settlement date for today's issue is April 25 and the</p>
<p>bills mature on May 23.</p>
<p>-- Vilnius newsroom, +370 2 223 517</p>
</text>
